@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Shipment Invoice Details and draft editor (FRO-366)
+
+Unmounted React UI for the approved Details/edit contract. This feature does not define a backend API, routes, authorization, monetary arithmetic, allocation, number generation, or persisted review state. Do not activate it until FRO-244/FRO-301 and the host integrations below are delivered.
+
+## Reuse and ownership
+
+The dependency is FRO-363 commit `230a90581aa85e611737add554b2b3c6f5912e0e`, prepared against main `5774931b9869247f0247013111a452552403f456`. Its 14 feature files were not on that main baseline. Integrate the create dependency first; this preparation includes its unchanged files at the original paths and compatibility-preserving extensions to the shared document/goods presentation.
+
+- [Document fields](../components/shipment-invoice-document-fields.tsx): existing portal controls, optional saved-reference fallback labels and separate Notes. Default ordinary-create layout remains unchanged.
+- [Goods](../components/shipment-invoice-goods.tsx): existing selection controls plus optional selected-only read mode and source row identity. Frozen reads never expose source refresh/allocation/selection.
+- [Selection](../create/selection.ts): existing identity operations, never financial calculations.
+- [Confirmations](../components/shipment-invoice-confirmations.tsx): existing Shipper and dirty-discard dialogs; lifecycle dialogs are separate.
+- [Details](../components/shipment-invoice-details.tsx): localized saved/read/edit composition over portal primitives. App shell and routing remain host-owned.
+- [Editor](use-invoice-editor.ts): TanStack Form saved values, selection, source/evaluation generation checks and dirty navigation.
+- [Actions](use-invoice-actions.ts): lifecycle, replacement and reconciliation orchestration. Separated from field state to keep action outcome handling reviewable.
+
+## Host contract
+
+[types.ts](types.ts) is a frontend presentation boundary, **not an API schema**. Supply authorized, localized values and authoritative action capabilities. Hidden or disabled buttons do not enforce authorization. No new authority enum has been introduced.
+
+`InvoiceRecordView` represents an authorized saved record. Draft reads must contain current source data and authoritative totals/review/finalization validation. Finalized/cancelled reads contain immutable, frozen fields, party text, selected row identities/values and totals. Supply formatted timestamps; `updatedLabel: null` means N/A. Keep display labels for saved references even when those references are no longer selectable. Dates in document values use ISO and display dd-mm-yyyy. Supply Europe/Athens `todayAthens` from the host; no browser-zone date default is inferred.
+
+Every callback receives or returns the types in `types.ts`; these cannot be wired by guessing an endpoint. Reads, eligibility, evaluation and all actions must enforce staff access/record scope in the backend. `actions.cancel` represents the backend's manager/system-admin decision. No browser role selector belongs in production.
+
+- `onRefreshGoods(id, revision)` supplies current Shipment/reference choices and row eligibility for a draft or replacement. Do not use frozen original rows as current replacement sources. Exclude this invoice from overlap evaluation.
+- `onEvaluateDraft(input)` supplies the full total, mixed-currency result, overlap identities, localized validation and opaque reviewed-state revision. Totals are never computed from formatted strings here. New source/selection/checked-field state must have a different review revision; stale persisted review must not be returned as valid.
+- `onSave(id, input)` permits incomplete otherwise-valid drafts and returns the saved record. Save does not issue a number. The UI excludes number/total/actor claims from the input.
+- `onFinalize(id, expectedRevision, reviewRevision)` must atomically verify required fields (including Agent), Shipment eligibility, selection and saved review; allocate exactly one number and freeze contents. Return the authoritative frozen record. Host `validationMessages` must be complete before the confirmation is available, and the operation must revalidate.
+- `onDiscard` and `onCancelInvoice` enforce lifecycle/permission/version guards. Cancellation requires a trimmed reason and preserves number and frozen contents. Discard success navigates to Shipment Details; cancelling unsaved editing never calls discard.
+- `onPrepareReplacement` is a read-only prefill. Copy approved document/party/manual fields and references, return current eligible rows, retain eligible selection order, identify invalid references and unavailable rows. UI locks the original Shipment and substitutes host-supplied todayAthens. Preparation/cancelling does not create a record.
+- `onCreateReplacement` is the only replacement write. Return the new identity (or record), unnumbered, with backend correction links in both directions; never alter original frozen values. The UI retains a successful destination so failed navigation cannot repeat creation.
+- `onReload` reads latest state. Conflicts retain local values, block commands and require explicit dirty-discard confirmation before reload. `onReconcile` resolves unknown outcomes without retrying mutations. While editing, reconciliation retains local work for comparison and requires reload before further writes.
+- `onOpenShipment` / `onOpenInvoice` supply real routes. Wire FRO-363 `onSaved(id)` to the same Details identity. No route is guessed or mounted here.
+- `onOpenAllocation(orderId)` must open the actual separately delivered Order allocation interface in a **new tab**. This feature never edits allocation. Missing integration leaves the allocation action disabled with an explanation.
+- `registerNavigationGuard` uses the create feature's guard contract. Route/back navigation must call the registered guard and only proceed through its continuation. The feature also guards its own links and browser close/reload while dirty/pending/uncertain.
+
+## Review, errors and concurrency
+
+Opening edit loads saved fields without creation defaults, locks Shipment and refreshes eligibility. New candidates remain unselected. Missing/ineligible saved rows are excluded from selection and identified in persistent local warnings. Fields survive refresh failures; dependent saves remain blocked until successful refresh and evaluation. Generation checks reject obsolete refresh/evaluation results, including after a different record is mounted.
+
+Confirm reviewed sends the current opaque revision with the next save; it never asserts backend persistence. Checked-field, selection and source changes invalidate acknowledgement. A matching saved read is required before finalization. Copied replacement packing, weight and partial amount remain visible for review. Incomplete review does not prevent saving unfinished work.
+
+`InvoiceActionResult` distinguishes known failure, validation, conflict and uncertain results. A thrown mutation is conservatively uncertain. The host must reconcile transport ambiguity, safe retries and duplicate prevention authoritatively. UI pending locks only prevent duplicate clicks in this mounted instance; they are not backend idempotency. Never automatically repeat a consequential operation after a timeout.
+
+## Local validation
+
+Fixtures in [**fixtures**/shipment-invoice-details.ts](__fixtures__/shipment-invoice-details.ts) and create fixtures are fictional and imported only by tests/isolated review hosts. The temporary browser host lives outside the delivered application tree. Use the application's ThemeProvider (compact), LabelsProvider and theme.css to review both EN/EL at 1440px and 400px. Exercise draft edits, source failures/review/mixed currencies/overlap, conflicts, all lifecycle dialogs and replacement identity navigation. Ordinary create regressions run alongside Details tests.
